From: Axiado Corporation <engineering@axiado.com>
Date: 2025-01-01 00:00:00
Subject: [PATCH] r52-compile-args: limit -ffreestanding to C and ASM only

GCC 13 arm-none-eabi in -ffreestanding C++ mode no longer exposes hosted
functions (malloc, free, etc.) from <cstdlib>/<stdlib.h>.  The C++ sources
in this project use hosted stdlib functions, so restrict -ffreestanding to
C and ASM compilation units only.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [GCC 13 toolchain compatibility fix]
Signed-off-by: Axiado Corporation <engineering@axiado.com>
---
--- a/base/r52-compile-args.cmake
+++ b/base/r52-compile-args.cmake
@@ -65,7 +65,8 @@
 add_compile_options(
 	-mcpu=${GCC_CPU}
 	-DCURRENT_CPU_ID=SVM_CPU_ID -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=${COMPILE_ARG_FILE}
-	-nostartfiles -nostdlib -g -ffreestanding -marm -fstack-protector-strong -mno-unaligned-access -fno-builtin
+	-nostartfiles -nostdlib -g -marm -fstack-protector-strong -mno-unaligned-access -fno-builtin
+	"$<$<NOT:$<COMPILE_LANGUAGE:CXX>>:-ffreestanding>"
 	"$<$<CONFIG:DEBUG>:-gdwarf-3>"
 	"$<$<COMPILE_LANGUAGE:CXX>:-fno-unwind-tables;-fno-rtti;-fno-exceptions>"
 	-fdata-sections
